# PROBE range-unsat. range(r) = C with C disjoint B makes A ⊑ ∃r.B unsatisfiable; B itself stays satisfiable.
# construct: ObjectPropertyRange
# expect: unsat :A
# expect-not: unsat :B

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty .
:r rdfs:range :C .
:C owl:disjointWith :B .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
